| Answering a host, rather than only being told by one.
|
| `code_event_fire` runs a handler and lets go of what it returned: an event
| is told, not asked. This is the other one — the answer is written back, and
| the host cannot go on without it.
|
| Nothing here fires or answers by itself; `tests/build_targets.rs` builds it
| for wasm and asks the questions. Run either ordinary way, the fixture proves
| that it compiles and leaks nothing.

| A guest wanting to draw somewhere, and a program deciding.
MayDraw { app, into } => {
    if app = "trusted" {
        return Allowed { into = "#guest-" + app }
    }
    return Refused { reason = "$app may not draw at $into" }
}

| An answer that is not an object at all — a host has to cope with that too.
Count { of } => {
    emit Length { value = of } to core get many
    return Counted { value = many.value }
}
